#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Social Desktop (Open Collaboration Services) settings module lets you "
"configure your user accounts for Open Collaboration Service Providers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the time of writing <ulink url=\"http://opendesktop.org/\">"
"openDesktop.org </ulink> is the first provider that you can use. You can use "
"the web site or this settings dialog to register and manage your account."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The benefit is that you can do more things in <quote>Get Hot New Stuff</quote>"
": vote for items, become a fan of them and upload new content. A configured "
"account also allows you to use the social Plasma widgets (<guilabel>"
"Community</guilabel>, <guilabel>Social News</guilabel> "
"&etc;) to their full extent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the &systemsettings; module:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select which provider to configure at the top. Either enter your "
"existing user name and password to let &kde; use them. You can verify that "
"these work by using the <guibutton>Test Login</guibutton> button"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you do not have an account yet, use the <guilabel>Register</guilabel> "
"tab. Here you need to fill out all fields. After clicking <guibutton>"
"Register...</guibutton> you will receive an email from the server to activate "
"your account."
msgstr ""


